= Concept — Simple =

A '''concept''' is an idea or unit of meaning that helps us think about things.

For example, "planet" is a concept.

Mars is an [[Entity/Simple|entity]] that fits the concept Planet.

The word "planet" is a label we use for the concept, but the word and the concept are not the same thing.

Different languages can use different words for similar concepts.

Concepts help us:
* recognize things;
* group things;
* reason;
* communicate;
* organize knowledge.

A [[Taxonomy/Simple|taxonomy]] can organize concepts into broader and narrower groups.

A knowledge system can also give each concept its own identifier and labels.

